Bundle stock contrib modules (pg_trgm) in the wheel

The wheel builds core Postgres + pgvector: pgbuild/Makefile runs `make install`,
which does not descend into contrib/ (that is `make install-world`). So the only
extensions a pgserver cluster can create are plpgsql and vector, and any schema
using a stock contrib module fails at `CREATE EXTENSION`:

    ERROR:  extension "pg_trgm" is not available
    DETAIL: Could not open extension control file ".../pg_trgm.control"

pg_trgm is the common case — trigram indexes back typo-tolerant search in a lot
of pgvector-adjacent applications, so it tends to sit right next to the vector
column the wheel already supports.

This builds the listed modules from the already-configured build tree, so it
needs no extra toolchain, no PGXS, and no sysroot handling: same compiler flags
and same install prefix as core. It runs before `fixup`, so macOS rpath
rewriting covers the new libraries too. Adds ~120 KB per platform.

CONTRIB_MODULES is a list, so other stock modules (btree_gin, pg_stat_statements,
citext, ...) are one word each if you want them.

Verified on macOS arm64 against PG 16.14: pg_trgm 1.6 creates, gin_trgm_ops
indexes build, and similarity() uses them. The hunks apply unchanged to the
v0.7.2 Makefile (PG 16.15).

--- a/pgbuild/Makefile
+++ b/pgbuild/Makefile
@@
 .PHONY: all
 all: fixup

 # Rewrite the absolute dylib install names Postgres bakes in to @rpath-relative form, so
 # the install tree is relocatable and PG16 + PG18 can coexist in one wheel without a
 # delocate basename collision (e.g. two libpq.5.dylib). No-op off macOS. Runs last, after
 # both postgres and pgvector have installed their libraries into $(INSTALL_PREFIX).
 .PHONY: fixup
-fixup: pgvector postgres
+fixup: pgvector contrib postgres
 	bash fixup_macos_rpaths.sh $(INSTALL_PREFIX)

 ### postgres
@@
 .PHONY: pgvector
 pgvector: postgres $(INSTALL_PREFIX)/lib/vector.so

+### contrib
+# Stock contrib modules. Core `make install` skips contrib/ entirely, so without
+# this the wheel can only offer plpgsql and vector. Built from the configured
+# build tree (not PGXS) so flags, prefix, and sysroot match core exactly.
+CONTRIB_MODULES := pg_trgm
+
+$(INSTALL_PREFIX)/share/postgresql/extension/pg_trgm.control: $(INSTALL_PREFIX)/bin/postgres
+	unset MAKELEVEL && unset MAKEFLAGS && unset MFLAGS \
+		&& for m in $(CONTRIB_MODULES); do \
+			$(MAKE) -C $(POSTGRES_BLD)/contrib/$$m -j install || exit 1; \
+		done
+
+.PHONY: contrib
+contrib: postgres $(INSTALL_PREFIX)/share/postgresql/extension/pg_trgm.control
+
 ### other
 .PHONY: clean clean-all
 clean:
